{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And you shall say to them.</b> A warning to the court (Sifrei)." "<b>Two for each day.</b> As its plain sense. But its main point comes to teach that they must be slaughtered opposite the day — the morning tamid toward the west and the afternoon tamid toward the east side of the rings (Sifrei; Yoma 62)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:05.366155573Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}